{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<staff-type>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"MXLStaffDetails.Kind","symbolKind":"enum","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"role":"symbol","extendedModule":"IvorMXL","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLStaffDetailsV4KindO"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails\/kind"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff-type value can be ossia, editorial, cue, alternate, or regular. An ossia staff represents music"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that can be played instead of what appears on the regular staff. An editorial staff also represents musical"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alternatives, but is created by an editor rather than the composer. It can be used for suggested"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interpretations or alternatives from other sources. A cue staff represents music from another part. An"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alternate staff shares the same music as the prior staff, but displayed differently (e.g., treble and bass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"clef, standard notation and tablature). It is not included in playback. An alternate staff provides more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"information to an application reading a file than encoding the same music in separate parts, so its use is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"preferred in this situation if feasible. A regular staff is the standard default staff-type.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind\/alternate","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind\/cue","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind\/editorial","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind\/ossia","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind\/regular"],"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","generated":true,"title":"Enumeration Cases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind\/Equatable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails/Kind/Equatable-Implementations":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails\/kind\/equatable-implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind\/Equatable-Implementations","title":"Equatable Implementations","abstract":[],"type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails/Kind":{"abstract":[{"text":"The staff-type value can be ossia, editorial, cue, alternate, or regular. An ossia staff represents music","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that can be played instead of what appears on the regular staff. An editorial staff also represents musical","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"alternatives, but is created by an editor rather than the composer. It can be used for suggested","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interpretations or alternatives from other sources. A cue staff represents music from another part. An","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"alternate staff shares the same music as the prior staff, but displayed differently (e.g., treble and bass","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"clef, standard notation and tablature). It is not included in playback. An alternate staff provides more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"information to an application reading a file than encoding the same music in separate parts, so its use is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"preferred in this situation if feasible. A regular staff is the standard default staff-type.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails\/kind","type":"topic","title":"MXLStaffDetails.Kind"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails/Kind/cue":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails\/kind\/cue","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A staff representing music from another part."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind\/cue","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cue","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"MXLStaffDetails.Kind.cue"},"doc://IvorMXL/s8CopyableP":{"title":"Swift.Copyable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP"},"doc://IvorMXL/SH":{"title":"Swift.Hashable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLStaffDetails","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff-details element is used to indicate different types of staves. The optional number attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies the staff number from top to bottom on the system, as with clef. The print-object attribute is used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to indicate when a staff is not printed in a part, usually in large scores where empty parts are omitted. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is yes by default. If print-spacing is yes while print-object is no, the score is printed in cutaway format"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where vertical space is left for the empty part."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP"},"doc://IvorMXL/s9EscapableP":{"title":"Swift.Escapable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP"},"doc://IvorMXL/SQ":{"title":"Swift.Equatable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails/Kind/alternate":{"fragments":[